This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and growth conditions for $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $f$, and we leverage a homotopy-based minimax principle to establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation. Additionally, we investigate the asymptotic behavior of this solution and demonstrate the compactness of Palais-Smale sequences. Moreover, we obtain a normalized ground state solution via a variational approach for the given equation. Furthermore, we normalize the ground state solution and establish the existence of a minimum norm ground state solution for the given equation. Lastly, we investigate the case where $\beta=0$ and provide a new proof for the existence of a ground state solution for the Choquard equation with exponential critical growth under certain constraints and growth conditions. Additionally, we discuss the impact of PS pspace on the existence of ground state solutions for the given equation. Moreover, we compare and contrast the results provided in this paper with the existing literature. Lastly, we present an open problem related to the given equation. 

For $\beta=0$, we recover the existing results from the literature. Moreover, we demonstrate the existence of a ground state solution for the given equation via a different approach. 

The main contribution of this paper is the investigation of the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation with exponential critical growth under certain constraints and growth conditions for $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $f$. 

